From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ntdll: no JIT pool dump for a UDF a guest image raises

ill_handler wrote the whole JIT pool, 896 MB, to the Documents folder at
the first illegal instruction of the app's life. World of Warcraft's
ARM64 client raises a UDF in its TLS callback at every start and
handles it, so each start wrote the file and dirtied every pool page.
A UDF in a guest image copy is now left out.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 5bb0598..2185874 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -11114,10 +11114,16 @@ static void ill_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *sigcontext )
             }
         }
         /* iOS-Madeira: also dump JIT pool here (the Mach UNHANDLED path may not
-         * fire for ILL since we deliver via setup_exception). One-shot. */
+         * fire for ILL since we deliver via setup_exception). One-shot.
+         * Playport (PLA-514): not for a UDF in a guest image, which the guest
+         * raises to handle it (World of Warcraft at every start): the dump
+         * wrote the whole pool, 896 MB, to the Documents folder each time. */
         {
+            extern uint64_t ios_jit_reverse_translate( uint64_t addr, uint64_t *module_base );
             static volatile int ill_dumped = 0;
-            if (__sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&ill_dumped, 0, 1)) {
+            int planned = !(pc & 3) && ios_jit_reverse_translate( pc, NULL ) &&
+                          !(*(const uint32_t *)(uintptr_t)pc >> 16);
+            if (!planned && __sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&ill_dumped, 0, 1)) {
                 extern void *ios_jit_rw_base_global;
                 extern size_t ios_jit_pool_size_global;
                 if (ios_jit_rw_base_global && ios_jit_pool_size_global) {
